Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 14:09:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 90/90] web-app: calendar messages, calendar tab, all-chats
 calendar, new events

Calendar messages (core/0036's `Calendar` viewtype) render as an event
card in the chat: a date badge, title, time, location, and repeating /
cancelled state. Clicking it shows the details with Open (the .ics) and
Show in chat. A draft with an .ics shows the same card in the composer,
like webxdc and vCard drafts do.

- Attachment menu: "Event" opens the event form and attaches the result as
  a draft, so the message text goes in the composer as usual. Picking an
  .ics file through "File" drafts it as Calendar too.
- A Calendar tab in the apps & media gallery shows the events core indexes:
  a month grid and an agenda list, with prev/next/today.
- All-chats calendar (account menu "Calendar", Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+Y): a sidebar
  lists the chats that have events with their counts; events are coloured
  by chat colour, and unticking a chat hides it (remembered per account in
  localStorage).
- Chat header: a calendar button next to apps & media opens the chat's
  calendar.
- "New event" in the calendar: title, all-day, start/end, repeat, location,
  description and an optional message; in the all-chats view a chat is
  picked first via the existing SelectChat dialog. Core writes the .ics
  (makeCalendarIcs) and it is sent as a Calendar message.
- Floating and all-day times come from core as wall-clock-in-UTC and are
  shown unshifted.
